%******************************************************************************
\chapter{Overview}
%******************************************************************************

\section{Architecture}

%claude:
[[chidb]] mirrors SQLite's layered design. Data flows top-to-bottom
through these layers, each aware only of the one below it: SQL text is
parsed into a [[chisql]] AST, optionally rewritten by the query
optimizer, compiled by the code generator into DBM bytecode, executed
by the database virtual machine against table/index cursors, which read
and write pages through B-Trees, which in turn read and write pages
through the pager, which reads and writes the [[chidb]] file itself.

